  "text": "Significance Level Significance Level a level In significance testing , the significance level is the highest value of a probability value for which the null hypothesis is rejected. Common significance levels are 0.05 and 0.01. If the 0.05 level is used, then the null hypothesis is rejected if the probability value is less than or equal to 0.05.",
